==Romanian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ro|ну||post-1930s (Moldovan) Cyrillic spelling}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ro|la|nōn}}. Compare {{cog|rup|nu}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ro|/nu/}}
* {{audio|ro|LL-Q7026 (cat)-Unjoanqualsevol-nu.wav}}
* {{rhyme|ro|u|s=1}}
* {{audio|ro|LL-Q7913 (ron)-Andreea Teodoraa-nu.wav}}

===Adverb===
{{head|ro|adverb}}

# [[no]]
# [[not]]

====Usage notes====
Romanian features the [[w:Double negative|double negative]]. ''{{lang|ro|Nu}}'' is stressed within a normal sentence, but in a double negative construction is left unstressed in favour of the other negative component.

In speech—even in moderately formal contexts—''{{lang|ro|nu}}'' is elided before verbs beginning with ''a'', most notably the past perfect auxiliary {{m|ro|avea}}.

Likewise, ''{{lang|ro|nu}}'' triggers [[prodelision]] before words (of any part of speech) beginning with ''î''. Elision and prodelision are orthographically marked with a hyphen where no [[line break]] may occur.

In these cases, the syllable following the ''n'' of ''{{lang|ro|nu}}'' takes the sentence stress, which is stronger than the primary stress of the negated word.

